    "model_version": "gemini-3.6-flash",
    "content": {
      "parts": [
        {
          "text": "# Renewal Approval Brief\n\n## Account snapshot\n\n- Customer: Northstar\n- Renewal date / days remaining: 10 days remaining\n- Current ARR: Missing (Requires input)\n- Requested discount: 18%\n- Dollar discount: Pending current ARR input\n- Proposed net ARR: Pending current ARR input\n- Churn risk: High\n\n## Customer requests\n\n- **18% discount** on renewal ARR (**requested**).\n- **Removal of auto-renewal clause** (**requested**).\n- Regulated customer compliance requirements.\n\n## Policy analysis\n\n- **Discount Approval Path**: The requested discount of 18% falls into the \"More than 15%\u201320%\" approval band. This requires sign-off from the Chief Revenue Officer and Finance Director. [Source: references/discount-policy.md]\n- **Renewal Timeline & Process**: With 10 days remaining until renewal (within the 14\u20130 days window), the team must execute a daily close plan. Because this is a high-risk and non-standard renewal, an assigned Executive owner is required. [Source: references/renewal-process.md]\n- **Non-Standard Contract Terms**: Removing auto-renewal language constitutes a non-standard contract change. Requests to remove or rewrite auto-renewal clauses must be routed to Legal. [Source: references/renewal-process.md, references/risk-escalation.md]\n- **High-Risk Escalation**: High churn risk with 30 days or less remaining (10 days) requires immediate escalation to an Executive sponsor and the Renewal Desk. [Source: references/risk-escalation.md]\n- **Regulated Customer Compliance**: As Northstar is a regulated customer, any new security, privacy, resilience, or compliance commitments requested by the customer must be routed to Security and Legal. [Source: references/risk-escalation.md]\n\n## Required approvals and escalations\n\n- **Commercial Approvals**: Route 18% discount request (**requested**) to the Chief Revenue Officer and Finance Director (**routed**).\n- **Legal Review**: Route auto-renewal removal request (**requested**) to Legal (**routed**).\n- **Executive & Renewal Desk Escalation**: Route high churn risk account escalation to the Executive sponsor and Renewal Desk (**routed**).\n- **Security & Legal Review**: Route any requested compliance, security, or privacy commitments to Security and Legal (**routed**).\n\n*(Note: None of the above requests are **approved** until the required authorities explicitly sign off.)*\n\n## Missing information\n\n- **Current ARR / List ARR**: Missing. Please provide the current ARR figure so the exact dollar discount amount and proposed net ARR can be computed using the quote calculator.\n\n## Recommended next actions\n\n1. **Activate Daily Close Plan**: Establish a daily close plan with the designated Executive owner and Renewal Desk given the 10-day window [Source: references/renewal-process.md].\n2. **Submit Approval & Escalation Requests**: Route the 18% discount request (**requested**) to the CRO and Finance Director, and submit the auto-renewal removal request (**requested**) to Legal [Source: references/discount-policy.md, references/risk-escalation.md].\n3. **Engage Executive Sponsor & Compliance**: Assign an Executive sponsor to engage Northstar leadership immediately, and coordinate with Security and Legal on any regulatory requirements [Source: references/risk-escalation.md].",
